{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Every lying object.</b> That which is designated for lying; one might think even if it is designated for another task — Scripture says ״אֲשֶׁר יִשְׁכַּב״ — not אֲשֶׁר שָׁכַב is said, but rather אֲשֶׁר יִשְׁכַּב — one designated always for this; this excludes that which they say to it, 'Stand up and let us do our work.'" "<b>Which one sits.</b> Not יָשַׁב is said, but rather ״אֲשֶׁר יֵשֵׁב עָלָיו״ — one designated always for this (Shabbat 59)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:32.785842666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}